WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.840
Hey, how are you, I'm Eddie.

00:00:00.840 --> 00:00:01.680
Hi, I'm Jessica.

00:00:01.680 --> 00:00:02.500
Nice to meet you.

00:00:02.500 --> 00:00:03.340
How are you?

00:00:03.340 --> 00:00:06.640
So Trump is defying the first, fourth, fifth.

00:00:06.640 --> 00:00:09.600
Fifth and 14th, and maybe the 22nd soon.

00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:13.600
Okay, so I wanna focus on the first and the fifth.

00:00:13.600 --> 00:00:14.440
Okay.

00:00:14.440 --> 00:00:18.200
So you say that Trump is defying the First Amendment.

00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:19.680
Can you give me an example?

00:00:19.680 --> 00:00:21.559
For example, he banned the Associated Press

00:00:21.559 --> 00:00:22.760
from attending White House events.

00:00:22.760 --> 00:00:23.879
A Trump-appointed judge said

00:00:23.879 --> 00:00:25.400
that was against the First Amendment.

00:00:25.400 --> 00:00:27.180
He's been cracking down on media organizations

00:00:27.180 --> 00:00:28.719
he doesn't like over their speech.

00:00:28.719 --> 00:00:30.360
If they say stuff he doesn't like,

00:00:30.360 --> 00:00:31.200
he, for example, he called-

00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:32.040
Cracking down how?

00:00:32.040 --> 00:00:34.099
So for example, he banned the Associated Press

00:00:34.099 --> 00:00:35.139
from attending White House events

00:00:35.139 --> 00:00:35.980
because they said-

00:00:35.980 --> 00:00:36.799
I can't go to the White House either.

00:00:36.799 --> 00:00:37.639
It's the Gulf of Mexico.

00:00:37.639 --> 00:00:38.480
That's not how it works.

00:00:38.480 --> 00:00:39.299
They were already at the White House.

00:00:39.299 --> 00:00:40.139
He deprived them for access,

00:00:40.139 --> 00:00:41.340
so he punished them for their speech.

00:00:41.340 --> 00:00:42.700
But are they allowed to go to the press?

00:00:42.700 --> 00:00:44.500
Which is why a judge he appointed,

00:00:44.500 --> 00:00:46.099
Trevor McFadden, said this was contrary

00:00:46.099 --> 00:00:46.959
to the First Amendment.

00:00:46.959 --> 00:00:48.540
A Trump-appointed judge.

00:00:48.540 --> 00:00:50.779
He's called MSNBC and CNN illegal.

00:00:50.779 --> 00:00:52.459
Media organizations are not ipso facto illegal.

00:00:52.459 --> 00:00:53.299
But that's free speech.

00:00:53.299 --> 00:00:54.380
He can call them whatever they want.

00:00:54.380 --> 00:00:55.660
Attacking the media?

00:00:55.660 --> 00:00:56.500
Yeah, he can attack them.

00:00:56.599 --> 00:00:57.639
As the executive?

00:00:57.639 --> 00:00:59.459
Yeah, he can say whatever he wants.

00:00:59.459 --> 00:01:00.680
That's literally the First Amendment.

00:01:00.680 --> 00:01:01.680
He can say whatever he wants.

00:01:01.680 --> 00:01:02.520
Absolutely.

00:01:02.520 --> 00:01:03.360
But the media can't say what they want.

00:01:03.360 --> 00:01:04.180
They do.

00:01:04.180 --> 00:01:05.019
But he's going after them.

00:01:05.019 --> 00:01:05.860
He's suing them.

00:01:05.860 --> 00:01:07.120
He's using lawsuits to crack down on the press.

00:01:07.120 --> 00:01:09.680
They used lawsuits to give him 34 felonies

00:01:09.680 --> 00:01:11.040
that Hillary Clinton did.

00:01:11.040 --> 00:01:12.440
No media gave him a lawsuit.

00:01:12.440 --> 00:01:14.360
No, but people on the Democratic side.

00:01:14.360 --> 00:01:15.320
We're not talking about the Democrats.

00:01:15.320 --> 00:01:16.160
Okay.

